9. Theorem I: Delayed Verification (Corrected)

9.1 Corrected Definition of the Guaranteed Domain

D18 (Geometric verification radius).

\rho_V(\tau_V):=L_x\tau_V+\varepsilon_V+\|\nu_V\|_\infty,

Remark 9.1. The probabilistic model error  \varepsilon_{\mathrm{model}}  from A2 does not appear in  \rho_V . It is a separate object and enters Theorem I as a residual risk bound, not as a geometric margin.

9.2 Corrected Guaranteed Domain

The earlier formulation of  \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{guaranteed}}  was under-specified because it depended only on the true state  x_t , ignoring the verifier estimate  \hat{x}_t^V . We correct this.

D18b (Guaranteed domain — corrected).

\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{guaranteed}}
:=
\left\{
x \in \mathcal{S}:
\forall \hat{x} \in B_{\rho_V}(x),\ 
\hat{x}\in\mathcal{S}\ \Longrightarrow\
\mathbb{P}(\phi(x_{t+1})=1 \mid \hat{x}, a\text{ approved})
\ge 1-\varepsilon_{\mathrm{model}}
\right\}.

This definition quantifies over all possible verifier estimates within the geometric uncertainty ball, ensuring that the guarantee holds for the true state regardless of which estimate the verifier happens to hold.

P2 (Sufficiency of the eroded safe set — corrected). Suppose A2 holds with model error  \varepsilon_{\mathrm{model}} . Let  x_t\in\mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V(\tau_V)} , and suppose the verifier estimate satisfies  \|\hat x_t^V-x_t\|\le\rho_V(\tau_V)  and  \hat x_t^V\in\mathcal{S} , and the verifier approves action  a . Then

\mathbb{P}\bigl(\phi(x_{t+1})=1\bigr)\ \ge\ 1-\varepsilon_{\mathrm{model}}.

Furthermore,

\mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V(\tau_V)}\subseteq\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{guaranteed}}.

Proof. Let  x_t\in\mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V} . By definition of erosion, every point of  B_{\rho_V}(x_t)  lies in  \mathcal{S} . Since  \|\hat x_t^V-x_t\|\le\rho_V , we have  \hat x_t^V\in B_{\rho_V}(x_t)\subseteq\mathcal{S} . The definition of  \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{guaranteed}}  then applies: for every  \hat{x}\in B_{\rho_V}(x_t)  with  \hat{x}\in\mathcal{S} , A2 gives  \mathbb{P}(\phi(x_{t+1})=1\mid \hat{x},a\text{ approved})\ge1-\varepsilon_{\mathrm{model}} . In particular, this holds for  \hat{x}=\hat{x}_t^V . The inclusion follows because the argument holds for every  x\in\mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V} .  \square 

Remark 9.2 (Why this is a sufficiency and not an equality). The converse inclusion  \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{guaranteed}}\subseteq\mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V}  requires three additional hypotheses: (i) the perception error can attain any direction in  B_{\rho_V} ; (ii) the verifier accepts exactly the estimates belonging to  \mathcal{S} , with no further margin; (iii) the filter introduces no additional robustness margin. Without these hypotheses, the correct statement is the sufficiency  \mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V}\subseteq\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{guaranteed}} , not the equality.

Corollary 9.1 (Equality under attainability). Suppose additionally that (i) the verifier's estimate error can realize any  v\in B_{\rho_V}  in some realization, (ii) the verifier's acceptance region is exactly  \mathcal{S}  up to the invariant boundary, and (iii) no additional filter margin is introduced. Then

\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{guaranteed}}=\mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V(\tau_V)}.

Corollary 9.2 (Monotone contraction).  \mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V(\tau_V)}  is nonincreasing in  \tau_V , with rate of contraction governed by  \mathrm{d}\rho_V/\mathrm{d}\tau_V=L_x .

P3 (Viability contraction under increasing verifier latency). Fix  \Theta_{\mathrm{des}}  and  \Theta_{\mathrm{pert}} . Let  \tau_V'\ge\tau_V , so that  \rho_V(\tau_V')\ge\rho_V(\tau_V)  and therefore

\mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V(\tau_V')}\subseteq\mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V(\tau_V)}.

Then

\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{rec}}\!\bigl(\Theta_{\mathrm{des}},\Theta_{\mathrm{pert}};\ \mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V(\tau_V')}\bigr)
\ \subseteq\
\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{rec}}\!\bigl(\Theta_{\mathrm{des}},\Theta_{\mathrm{pert}};\ \mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V(\tau_V)}\bigr).

Proof. By Corollary 9.2, the eroded safe sets are nested. Apply Lemma 8.1 with  \mathcal{S}_1=\mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V(\tau_V')}  and  \mathcal{S}_2=\mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V(\tau_V)} .  \square 

Remark 9.3 (Chain of results). The chain

\tau_V\uparrow\ \Longrightarrow\ \rho_V\uparrow\ \Longrightarrow\ \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{eff}}\downarrow\ \Longrightarrow\ \mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{rec}}\downarrow

is a composition of three separately proved statements: the definition of  \rho_V  and Lemma 4.1, Corollary 9.2, and Lemma 8.1 followed by P3.

Theorem I (Delayed verification — corrected). Under A2, Lemma 4.1, and the definitions of §9, the verifier's guaranteed domain contains the erosion  \mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V(\tau_V)} , the guaranteed next-step invariant holds with probability at least  1-\varepsilon_{\mathrm{model}} , and the viability kernel is monotone nonincreasing in  \tau_V .

