14. Robustness and Extensions

Remark 14.1 (Model error inside the verifier). A2 introduces  \varepsilon_{\mathrm{model}}  as a residual probability. Deriving  \varepsilon_{\mathrm{model}}  from explicit model-mismatch bounds on the transition kernel is an open problem.

Remark 14.2 (Degenerate boundary locus). The transversality condition  \|\nabla_{\Theta_{\mathrm{pert}}}A\|\ge g>0  fails near points where the gradient vanishes or where multiple constraints become simultaneously active.

Remark 14.3 (Violations of A7). Systems in which irreversibility alters the instantaneous invariant violate A7 and may exhibit non-monotone gap behaviour.

Remark 14.4 (Dependence between nominal and failure disturbances). Relaxing A1 introduces dependence between  \eta^{\mathrm{nom}}  and  \eta^{\mathrm{fail}} . The structural results remain valid provided A2 is re-examined under the enlarged class.

Remark 14.5 (Verifier fallback policy — open problem). Whether the fallback-induced contraction can be completely bounded by an expanded geometric margin remains open (P8 addresses the negative direction).

