Appendix G: Backup Control Barrier Functions

G.1 Control Barrier Functions

G.1.1 (CBF). A continuously differentiable function  h:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}  is a control barrier function for the safe set  \mathcal{C}=\{x:h(x)\ge0\}  if there exists a class- \mathcal{K}  function  \alpha  such that

\sup_{u\in U}\bigl[L_f h(x)+L_g h(x)u+\alpha(h(x))\bigr]\ge 0

for all  x\in\mathcal{C} .

G.1.2 (Safety guarantee). If  h  is a CBF and  u  satisfies the CBF condition, then  \mathcal{C}  is forward invariant.

G.2 Backup CBF

G.2.1 (Backup policy). Let  \pi_{\mathrm{fb}}:\mathcal{X}\to U  be a backup policy.

G.2.2 (Backup trajectory). For initial state  x , the backup trajectory is the solution of

\dot x_{\mathrm{fb}}(t)=f(x_{\mathrm{fb}}(t),\pi_{\mathrm{fb}}(x_{\mathrm{fb}}(t))),\qquad x_{\mathrm{fb}}(0)=x.

G.2.3 (Backup CBF). The backup CBF is

h_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x)=\min_{t\in[0,T_{\mathrm{fb}}]}h(x_{\mathrm{fb}}(t)),

where  T_{\mathrm{fb}}  is the backup horizon.

G.2.4 (Implicit safe set). The implicit safe set induced by the backup policy is

\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{fb}}=\{x\in\mathcal{S}:h_{\mathrm{BCBF}}(x)\ge0\}.

G.2.5 (Structural distinction).  \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{fb}}  is generally a strict subset of  \mathcal{S} , and its geometry depends on  \pi_{\mathrm{fb}} , not only on  \mathcal{S} .

G.3 Proof of P8 (Non-Absorbability of Fallback Contraction)

P8. The fallback-induced contraction of the viability kernel cannot in general be absorbed into the geometric erosion  \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{eff}} .

Proof. Suppose, for contradiction, that there exists  \rho'\ge\rho_V(\tau_V)  such that

\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{rec}}(\mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho'})=\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{rec}}^{\pi_{\mathrm{fb}}}(\mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V(\tau_V)})

for all admissible  \pi_{\mathrm{fb}} . The left-hand side depends only on the geometry of  \mathcal{S}  and  \rho' . The right-hand side depends on  \pi_{\mathrm{fb}}  through the closed-loop dynamics. Fix  \mathcal{S}  and  \rho_V . Choose two backup policies  \pi_{\mathrm{fb}}^1,\pi_{\mathrm{fb}}^2  such that  \mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{fb}}^1\neq\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{fb}}^2 . Then

\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{rec}}^{\pi_{\mathrm{fb}}^1}(\mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V})\neq\mathcal{K}_{\mathrm{rec}}^{\pi_{\mathrm{fb}}^2}(\mathcal{S}\ominus B_{\rho_V})

for some constraint geometry, while the left-hand side is identical for both. Contradiction. Hence no single  \rho'  can equalize the two for all  \pi_{\mathrm{fb}} .  \square 

G.3.1 (Remark). The proof assumes the existence of two backup policies inducing distinct implicit safe sets. This is generically true; degenerate cases where all backup policies induce the same safe set are excluded.

