Appendix H: Technical Lemmas and Auxiliary Results

H.1 Lipschitz Continuity of the Violation Probability

H.1.1 (Assumption). Suppose  A(\Theta_{\mathrm{pert}})  is  L_A -Lipschitz in  \Theta_{\mathrm{pert}}  with respect to the Euclidean norm.

H.1.2 (Boundary displacement). Under H.1.1, the Hausdorff distance between  \partial\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\Theta_{\mathrm{des}})  and  \partial\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\Theta_{\mathrm{des}}')  is bounded by  L_A\|\Theta_{\mathrm{des}}-\Theta_{\mathrm{des}}'\| .

Proof. The level set  \{A=\epsilon\}  moves continuously with  A . The Lipschitz constant controls the displacement.  \square 

H.2 Transversality Condition

H.2.1 (Transversality). Assume  \|\nabla_{\Theta_{\mathrm{pert}}}A\|\ge g>0  on  \partial\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{safe}} .

H.2.2 (Implicit function theorem). Under H.2.1,  \partial\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{safe}}  is a  C^1  manifold of codimension 1.

H.2.3 (Local displacement). The local displacement of  \partial\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{safe}}  under a perturbation  \delta\Theta_{\mathrm{des}}  is

\delta\Theta_{\mathrm{pert}}=-\frac{\nabla_{\Theta_{\mathrm{des}}}A\cdot\delta\Theta_{\mathrm{des}}}{\|\nabla_{\Theta_{\mathrm{pert}}}A\|^2}\nabla_{\Theta_{\mathrm{pert}}}A.

Proof. Apply the implicit function theorem to  A(\Theta_{\mathrm{pert}};\Theta_{\mathrm{des}})=\epsilon .  \square 

H.3 Degenerate Boundary Locus

H.3.1 (Degenerate set). Define

\mathcal{D}=\{\Theta_{\mathrm{pert}}\in\partial\mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{safe}}:\|\nabla_{\Theta_{\mathrm{pert}}}A\|<g\}.

H.3.2 (Open problem). Whether  \mu(\mathcal{D})=0  under the reference measure  \mu  is open. If  \mu(\mathcal{D})>0 , the boundary may jump discontinuously.

H.4 Projection Error Bound

H.4.1 (Lipschitz projections). Suppose  \sigma_D,\sigma_F,\sigma_U  are  L_\sigma -Lipschitz.

H.4.2 (Conjectured bound).

|\mathcal{I}_{123}-\tilde\Delta_{DFU}|\le C L_\sigma\|\Theta_{\mathrm{pert}}\|,

where  C  depends on the smoothness of  A .

H.4.3 (Status). This bound is conjectural. Closing this gap is Open Problem 10.

H.5 Coupling of Design and Perturbation

H.5.1 (A3 separation).  \Theta_{\mathrm{des}}  and  \Theta_{\mathrm{pert}}  are formally disjoint.

H.5.2 (Consequence). Every statement about the safety landscape is a statement about  \mathcal{R}_{\mathrm{safe}}(\Theta_{\mathrm{des}})  as a function of  \Theta_{\mathrm{pert}}  for fixed  \Theta_{\mathrm{des}} .

H.5.3 (Violation). If design and perturbation coordinates are mixed, interaction effects are uninterpretable. This is the core methodological commitment of CVA-Space.

